   "text": "This is a rifamycin\u2011type ansamycin in which the naphthoquinone core is fused to a bromo\u2011substituted phenoxazine. I read it region by region and wrote the SMILES from that reading.\n\n**Core.**\n- The furanone ring carries a quaternary carbon with a methyl (hashed bond) and a wedged O\u2011vinyl ether link to the ansa chain.\n- The aromatic ring bears CH3 and OH.\n- The quinone ring has a C=O and an NH\u2011acyl group.\n- The phenoxazine has one C=N and one ring O. The Br sits para to the ring\u2011O\u2011bearing carbon.\n\n**Ansa chain.** From the vinyl ether the chain runs:\n- O\u2013CH=CH (E)\n- CH(OMe)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OAc)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OH)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OH)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH=CH (E)\n- CH=C(CH3) (Z)\n- C(=O)NH\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I assigned each centre from its wedge or hash. The H on each centre points opposite the wedged or hashed substituent. The three double bonds are the two E alkenes and the Z alkene (carbonyl cis to the chain CH) described above. This was done by hand from the 2D coordinates, so the individual @/@@ assignments are the least certain part.\n\nSMILES: C[C@]12O/C=C/[C@@H](OC)[C@H](C)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@H](O)[C@H](C)/C=C/C=C(C)\\C(=O)Nc3c4oc5ccc(Br)cc5nc4c4c(c3=O)c(O)c(C)c(O1)c4C2=O"
  }
